{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "italic"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Question from Fall 2022 Stanford Midterm",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "We are going to build a Bayesian Viral Load Test which updates a belief distribution regarding a patient's viral load. Though viral load is continuous, in our test we represent it by discretizing the quantity into whole numbers between 0 and 99, inclusive. The units of viral load are the number of viral instances per million samples.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If a person has a viral load of 9 (in other words, 9 viruses out of every 1 million samples) what is the probability that a random sample from the person is a virus?",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{9}{1,000,000}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "We test 100,000 samples from one person for the virus. If the person's true viral load is 9, what is the probability that exactly 1 of our 100,000 samples is a virus? Use a computationally efficient approximation to compute your answer. Your approximation should respect that there is 0 probability of getting negative virus samples.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let's define a random variable ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ", the number of samples that are viral given the true viral load is 9. The question is asking for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\P(X=1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". We can think about this as a binomial process, where the number of trials is the number of samples and the probability is the probability that a sample is viral.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nn = 100,000,\\;\\; p = \\frac{9}{1,000,000}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Notice that ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "p"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " is very small and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " is very large, so we can use the Poisson approximation to approximate our answer. We find ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\lambda = np = 100,000 \\cdot 9/1,000,000 = 0.9"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ", so ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\text{Poi}(\\lambda = 0.9)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". The last step is to use the PMF of the Poisson distribution.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nP(X = 1) = \\frac{(0.9)^1 e^{-0.9}}{1!}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Based on what we know about a patient (their symptoms and personal history) we have encoded a prior belief in a list ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "style": "rgb(232, 62, 140)"
       },
       "type": "code"
      }
     ],
     "text": "prior",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " where ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "style": "rgb(232, 62, 140)"
       },
       "type": "code"
      }
     ],
     "text": "prior[i]",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " is the probability that the viral load equals ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "style": "rgb(232, 62, 140)"
       },
       "type": "code"
      }
     ],
     "text": "prior",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " is of length 100 and has keys 0 through 99.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Write an equation for the updated probability that the true viral load is ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " given that we observe a count of 1 virus sample out of 100,000 tested. Recall that ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "0 \\leq i \\leq 99"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". You may use approximations.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "V"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be the viral load of the patient.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be the observed samples that are viral out of 100,000",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "We want to find",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    \\P(V= i | X = 1)\n\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "We can apply Bayes Rule to get ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n   \\P(V= i | X = 1) = \\frac{\\P(X=1 | V = i) \\cdot \\P(V = i)}{\\P(X = 1)}\n\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "If we know the true viral load, we know the probability of each sample being viral. As such ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " is a binomial:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nX \\sim \\Bin(n=100000,\\;\\; p = \\frac{i}{1000000})\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "We can approximate ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "as a Poisson! Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": " approximation to a binomial with ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n=100000"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "p = \\frac{i}{1000000}"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\lambda = np = 100000 \\cdot \\frac{i}{1000000} = \\frac{i}{10}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " can be written as ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y\\sim \\Poi(\\lambda = \\frac{i}{10})"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". Now we can solve for the first term in our Bayes Rule expression:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nP(X=1|V=i) &\\approx P(Y=1|V=i)\\\\\n&\\approx \\frac{\\frac{i}{10}e^{\\frac{-i}{10}}}{1!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{i}{10}e^{\\frac{-i}{10}}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Lets plug that result in:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n   \\P&(V= i | X = 1) \\\\\n   &= \\frac{\\P(X=1 | V = i) \\cdot \\P(V = i)}{\\P(X = 1)}\\\\\n   &= \\frac{\\frac{i}{10}e^{-\\frac{i}{10}} \\cdot \\P(V = i)}{\\P(X=1)}\\\\\n   &= \\frac{\\frac{i}{10}e^{-\\frac{i}{10}} \\cdot \\texttt{prior[i]}}{\\P(X=1)}\\\\\n   &= \\frac{\\frac{i}{10}e^{-\\frac{i}{10}} \\cdot \\texttt{prior[i]}}{\n   \\sum\\limits_{j=0}^{99} \\frac{j}{10}e^{-\\frac{j}{10}} \\cdot \\texttt{prior[j]}\n   }\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Note the last line uses the general law of total probability",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
